--- a/docs/agents/mcp-tools.md
+++ b/docs/agents/mcp-tools.md
@@ -142,4 +142,4 @@ The server lists 138 tools. The live `tools/list` reply is the authority; this f
 | `set_tool_assembly` | `links`, `tool` | Set a document tool's component assembly, root first: links is [{component, mount?: {parent, port?, z_rot_deg?, projection_mm?}}] (no mount: the root, on the spindle; parent is a node index). The derived tool record (diameter, corner radius, or a solid tool's own record) and the holder body land in one undo step, and the tool's operations go stale. links null clears the assembly and keeps the tool's records. Refused by name: an unknown or non-tool name, an unknown key, an empty links, a component the document does not hold, a component that does not fit its parent (the property is named), a bad port, frame or stickout, a lathe-held tool, a body in the flutes, and a change that an operation of the tool cannot take. |
 | `save_library_component` | `component?`, `id?`, `library?` | Save a tool component to the user's component library: a document component by id, or a full component (the component object of a list_tool_components row). An entry with the same id is replaced. A file edit, not a document change: no undo step. Refused by name: both or neither of id and component, an id the document does not hold, a builtin: id (built-in components are read only), a component that states library_ref, and every component check. |
 | `delete_library_component` | `id`, `library?` | Delete a tool component from the user's component library. A file edit, not a document change: no undo step. Document components linked to it then show the sync status missing_from_library. Refused by name: a builtin: id (built-in components are read only) and an id the library does not hold. |
-| `edit_user_holder` | `bore?`, `clamp?`, `gauge_len?`, `id`, `largest_d?`, `name?`, `nose_d?`, `taper?` | Edit a holder of the document's component table by its shape, as the holder form does: taper, clamp, bore, gauge_len, nose_d, largest_d and name. A field the call does not state keeps the holder's value (an ER or Weldon clamp without largest_d takes nose_d: it has one body diameter). The outline is the holder library's outline of the shape, never smaller than the stated steel. Every tool whose assembly uses the holder is derived again in the same undo step. One undo step. Refused by name: an id the document does not hold, a holder whose outline is not a shape outline (use upsert_tool_component), an unknown taper or clamp, a value that cannot describe steel, an empty name, an edit that changes nothing, and an edit that a tool built from the holder cannot take (the tool is named; nothing changes). |
+| `edit_user_holder` | `bore?`, `clamp?`, `gauge_len?`, `id`, `largest_d?`, `name?`, `nose_d?`, `taper?` | Edit a holder of the document's component table by its shape, as the holder form does: taper, clamp, bore, gauge_len, nose_d, largest_d and name. A field the call does not state keeps the holder's value (an ER or Weldon clamp without largest_d takes nose_d: it has one body diameter). The outline is the holder library's outline of the shape, never smaller than the stated steel. Every tool whose assembly uses the holder is derived again in the same undo step. One undo step. Refused by name: an id the document does not hold, a holder whose outline is not a shape outline (use upsert_tool_component), an unknown taper or clamp, a value that cannot describe steel, a shrink-fit body that the flange envelope covers at that gauge length (the outline cannot keep it: give a longer gauge length), an empty name, an edit that changes nothing, and an edit that a tool built from the holder cannot take (the tool is named; nothing changes). |

